MODULE state

FUNCTION ensure state directories
    create package store, digest cache, receipt, and recoverable-trash roots
        only through contained paths without symbolic-link components
    require the Portprog-owned Go module boundary directly under install_root,
        creating it when absent and rejecting foreign content without overwrite

FUNCTION read or write lockfile and receipt
    strictly decode or encode the schema in SPEC.md
    validate all fields, UTC timestamps, dependency order, and portable paths
    write through a synchronized temporary file
    preserve any prior state file in local trash
    atomically publish the new file and restore the prior file if publication
        fails

FUNCTION move path to trash
    require the source to be a child of the Portprog base directory
    choose a unique UTC-stamped destination beneath the trash root
    rename the source there and return the recovery path

FUNCTION determine package health
    compare lock package, receipt, platform, source, checksum, exact store path, and
        every expected executable
    return installed, missing, outdated, or damaged with an explanation
